  1. Install base dependencies:
  sudo apt-get install -y build-essential libssl-dev libnghttp2-dev zlib1g-dev libcjson-dev

  2. Build & install a current cJSON from source (Ubuntu's packaged cJSON is too old — your code needs the newer bool-returning API):
  cd /tmp
  git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/DaveGamble/cJSON.git
  cd cJSON && mkdir build && cd build
  cmake .. -DENABLE_CJSON_UTILS=Off -DENABLE_CJSON_TEST=Off -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr/local
  make -j4
  sudo make install
  sudo ldconfig

  3. Build seppd itself, pointing at OpenSSL 3.5 (system default is 1.1.1, too old for SSL_get1_peer_certificate):
  cd /home/mhoang/Desktop/Mantis/sepp/seppd
  OPENSSL_CFLAGS="-I/opt/openssl-3.5/include" \
  OPENSSL_LDFLAGS="-L/opt/openssl-3.5/lib64 -Wl,-rpath,/opt/openssl-3.5/lib64 -lssl -lcrypto" \
  make

  4. Verify:
  ls -la seppd
  ldd seppd
  You should see a seppd binary in the directory, linking against /opt/openssl-3.5/lib64/libssl.so.3 and /usr/local/lib/libcjson.so.1 with no missing libraries.

